{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-planck-time","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:planck-time","kind":"definition","title":"Planck Time","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-planck-constant"],"tags":["planck-time","discrete-time","reeb-flow","information-theory"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.planckTime","text":"planck-time.md","leanSource":"planck-time.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:planck-time\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Planck Time</em></p>\n<p><strong>Definition.</strong>\nLet <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in k^\\times \\setminus \\{1\\}</code> denote the substrate parameter (<a href=\"#def:substrate-parameter\">substrate parameter</a>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q = 1 - q^{-1}</code> denote the quantum Planck constant (<a href=\"#def:quantum-planck-constant\">quantum Planck constant</a>). We define the <strong>Planck time</strong> as</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  t_P(q)  :=  \\frac{1}{\\hbar_q}\n  =  \\frac{q}{q - 1}.</code></pre>\n<p>This rational function of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is defined over any field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\neq 1</code>.</p>\n"}
